# Everything here runs on Linux, and two of these files are executed by a
# shell. Checked out with CRLF - which git does by default on a Windows clone,
# and which this repository has no reason to want anywhere - the shebang
# becomes "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r" and the kernel answers "bad interpreter".
#
# vklayer-run is the one that matters most: the build copies it into the
# AppImage verbatim and Steam runs it in front of the game, so a CRLF checkout
# produces a package whose launch option fails at the moment somebody starts
# playing. It happened - the first AppImage built here shipped exactly that.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
AppRun      text eol=lf
vklayer-run text eol=lf

*.png binary
